{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_sample`, `y_spec`, `y_sens`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 1)` priors for the bounded parameters `p`, `spec`, and `sens` before their first use in the model block. These priors are density-neutral relative to the original finite `[0, 1]` parameter constraints. The observed/protected variables are each scored exactly once by built-in `binomial` sampling statements. No data changes were made; `n_sample`, `n_spec`, and `n_sens` remain unprotected context counts.
","model_safe_stan":"/**
 * meta-analysis over studies of disease infection rate 
 * for variation in sensitivity and specificity
 * pool data from all studies
 */
data {
  int y_sample;
  int n_sample;
  int y_spec;
  int n_spec;
  int y_sens;
  int n_sens;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=1> p;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> spec;
  real<lower=0, upper=1> sens;
}
model {
  real p_sample;
  p ~ uniform(0, 1);
  spec ~ uniform(0, 1);
  sens ~ uniform(0, 1);
  p_sample = p * sens + (1 - p) * (1 - spec);
  y_sample ~ binomial(n_sample, p_sample);
  y_spec ~ binomial(n_spec, spec);
  y_sens ~ binomial(n_sens, sens);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"n_sample":6,"n_sens":4,"n_spec":2,"y_sample":4,"y_sens":3,"y_spec":2}","protected_variables":["y_sample","y_spec","y_sens"]}
